            <ArticleTitle>Measuring patients' perceptions of nursing care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32B-D</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Each year pain disables approximately 50 million Americans. This study determined the relationships among pain management and patients' and nurses' perceptions of quality nursing care. This study was a secondary analysis of data for 91 patients, with additional data collected. How patients perceive their nursing care may correlate with how well their pain is managed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
